From ac37ae77834230b71da8a080b46650305cff06d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:55:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] dt-bindings: clock: add the Hi3716CV200 CRG ids

The Hi3716CV200 core CRG needs its clock ids published. Number the ids
by (register offset, field low bit) over the fields the register
descriptions name, the way the Hi3798MV100 header does, append-only so
describing another block later cannot renumber an existing one. Only
fields whose consumer is driven by this port are published, together
with the fixed sources the driver registers for the gates that divide
their parent; the one clock modelled as a rate rather than a gate is
described from the per-mode display register pairs, because no authority
states what the hpll_ctrl0 fields mean on this part. Add the id header.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 .../clock/hisilicon,hi3716cv200-crg.h         | 313 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 313 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3716cv200-crg.h

--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3716cv200-crg.h
@@ -0,0 +1,313 @@
